  "description": "Run the pinned resumable campaign and commit its versioned evidence receipt with a concise provenance record.\n\n## Background\n\nThe scientific target is the pinned Fossorier 1994 dissertation series [Fossorier1994] for eBCH $(128,64)$ on BI-AWGN/BPSK: order-2 BER versus $E_b/N_0$, with order 1 as an explicitly internal control. The [Fossorier1995] article is closed-access and recorded as unverified. Measurements remain valid or falsifying according to confidence intervals and recorded protocol identity.\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [hard] REQ-01: The committed receipt records seeds, git revision, toolchain, hardware, configuration, per-cell counts, work counters, termination, and binomial confidence intervals.\n- [hard] REQ-02: Each matched order-2 point accepts its published value $p$ exactly when $p \\in [L \\cdot 10^{-\\delta}, U \\cdot 10^{+\\delta}]$, where $[L, U]$ is the receipt interval at its recorded method and level and $\\delta$ the recorded digitization precision in $\\log_{10}$ decades, without converting discrepancies into silent retuning.\n- [hard] REQ-03: Order-1 results are identified as campaign controls rather than externally sourced claims.\n- [hard] REQ-04: Interrupted, censored, or budget-exhausted cells remain visible and resumable without repeated completed work.\n- [hard] REQ-05: The provenance note identifies contradictory evidence and the exact receipt schema version.\n- [hard] REQ-06: Committed figures plot the order-2 comparison and the order-1 control series (estimates with confidence intervals against the published values), generated deterministically from the receipt and dataset by a committed script, and linked to this issue as documents.",
